or-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\" alt=\"Explain Change →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Walkthrough</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\nThe changes add badge update management and utilities for selecting existing app windows, matching installed apps to URLs, and grouping tabs by app, preset, active domain, or hostname.\n\n**Changes: Badge updates**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Badge state and updates** <br> `background/badge.js`|The module adds busy-state control and action-popup selection. It reads the configured window scope to count matching tabs, updates the badge, and schedules delayed updates. |\n\n**Window matching and tab grouping**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Window and app matching** <br> `utils/window-matcher.js`|The module selects an exact-URL or same-domain app or popup window. It also matches eligible installed apps to valid HTTP(S) URLs. |\n|**Tab grouping** <br> `utils/window-matcher.js`|The module groups valid tabs by installed app, preset, active domain, or hostname. It fills missing icons from tab favicons and sorts groups by tab count. |\n\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Estimated code review effort:** 3 (Moderate) | ~20 minutes\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"9b4b58f7aa664e3cbf77b9ba760027be15d72e55\" -->\n<!-- change_assessment_priority:{\"version\":1,\"urgency\":\"p3\",\"manual\":false} -->\n**Change:** Other\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-low-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Low</strong> · up to <code>9b4b5</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **🔵 Low** · up to `9b4b5`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"9b4b58f7aa664e3cbf77b9ba760027be15d72e55\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"9b4b58f7aa664e3cbf77b9ba760027be15d72e55\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThe new window-matching and badge helpers have several small correctness gaps: case-distinct URLs can be treated as duplicates, apps can be matched by name despite explicit domains, some installed apps are not grouped, and the badge count can briefly be stale. None is severe or hard to recover from, but they are worth fixing if this code is ever adopted. The PR is marked as an experiment and not for merge.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Pre-merge checks: <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-passed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Passed\" title=\"Passed\"></picture></sup> 3 · <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-failed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Failed\" title=\"Failed\"></picture></sup> 1</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<strong><sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-failed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Failed\" title=\"Failed\"></picture></sup> Failed checks: 1 warning</strong>\n\n|  Check name |                                              Status                                              | Explanation                                                                                                                                                            